{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאבק", :translit "v'yei'aveik", :gloss "and he wrestled"} {:he "כסא הכבוד", :translit "kisei ha-kavod", :gloss "Throne of Glory"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויאבק", :b "כסא הכבוד"}], :frame {:text "The word ויאבק (Genesis 32:25) is read as related to אבק, dust. By equating it in gematria with כסא הכבוד, the comment conveys that the dust of the wrestling rose all the way to the heavenly Throne. The Throne of Glory is God's throne in heaven, named in 1 Samuel 2:8 and Jeremiah 17:12.", :sources ["Genesis 32:25" "1 Samuel 2:8" "Jeremiah 17:12"]}} {:quotes [{:he "איש עמו", :translit "ish imo", :gloss "a man with him"} {:he "עשו אדום", :translit "esav edom", :gloss "Esav Edom"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "איש עמו", :b "עשו אדום"}], :frame {:text "Genesis 32:25 records that יעקב wrestled with an איש, a man. The equating of איש עמו with עשו אדום in gematria identifies the mysterious adversary as connected to Esav. The next verse, Genesis 32:26, states that the assailant was unable to prevail, suggesting an adversary of cosmic significance.", :sources ["Genesis 32:25" "Genesis 32:26"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויאבק איש עמו", :translit "v'yei'aveik ish imo", :gloss "and he wrestled a man with him"} {:he "קשו", :translit "kasho", :gloss "his stubble"} {:he "עשו", :translit "esav", :gloss "Esav"} {:he "קש", :translit "kash", :gloss "stubble"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "ויאבק איש עמו", :spells "קשו"}], :frame {:text "Obadiah 1:18 foretells that the house of יעקב shall be a fire and the house of יוסף a flame, while the house of עשו becomes לקש, stubble. The application of stubble imagery to the house of Esav is thus rooted in this prophecy.", :sources ["Obadiah 1:18"]}}], :arithmetic [{:a-value 119, :b-value 118, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "כסא הכבוד", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "ויאבק"} {:kind :gematria, :a "איש עמו", :a-value 427, :b "עשו אדום", :b-value 427, :lens :